messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/pds/tif_pdsdirread.c
Line: 609
Function: TIFFFetchShortPair
Bug type: stack-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-121
Explanation: Passes a 2-element stack array v[2] to TIFFFetchByteArray(), which will write up to 4 elements when dir->tdir_count is 3 or 4 (due to switch fall-through). This overflows v (writes v[2], v[3]) when a crafted tag has BYTE/SBYTE type with count > 2.

Source context:
```c
      569:             switch (dir->tdir_count)
      570:             {
      571:                 case 2:
      572:                     v[1] = dir->tdir_offset & 0xffff;
      573:                 case 1:
      574:                     v[0] = dir->tdir_offset >> 16;
      575:             }
      576:         }
      577:         else
      578:         {
      579:             switch (dir->tdir_count)
      580:             {
      581:                 case 2:
      582:                     v[1] = dir->tdir_offset >> 16;
      583:                 case 1:
      584:                     v[0] = dir->tdir_offset & 0xffff;
      585:             }
      586:         }
      587:         return (1);
      588:     }
      589:     else
      590:         return (TIFFFetchData(tif, dir, (char *)v) != 0);
      591: }
